+/*
+ * nuwa observation only (XNU_NUWA_OBSERVE). Two frame-buffer bands, painted
+ * once each: band 3 (cyan, rows 3/16..4/16) when initproc's exec completed and
+ * band 15 (orange, last 1/16) on initproc's first BSD syscall. Bands 1 and 2
+ * (blue, magenta) belong to the build's MMU-off / MMU-on entry markers.
+ *
+ * Plus a readable event log: a 14-line grid in the middle of the screen
+ * (rows from 1/2 height, 42 px apart, 5x12 glyphs scaled 3) drawn with the same
+ * font the panic screen uses. Every emitter writes one line and repaints only
+ * that line box, so an event costs one 42-row clear plus the glyph stores.
+ * All of it is stores to vinfo.v_baseaddr: no lock, no allocation, no sleep,
+ * no call out. Concurrent CPUs may interleave or lose a line; that is fine.
+ */
